--- A parsed value — a document's member — is read as the kind its use
--- implies, in both modes (spec, JSON): a position an int, a key text,
--- one met in arithmetic or an order a float, one compared with text
--- text, one decided on, negated or joined with and/or a bool, one met
--- beside a moment a moment, one handed to a builtin what its rows take,
--- one assigned to a variable of a kind that kind, and one handed to a
--- function what the function's body reads of it. Nothing is read first
--- by hand. (Each had been refused until read; a parsed value decided on,
--- negated or joined with and had run interpreted and not built
--- compiled.) What is not what the program reads stops with what it
--- holds and the read that asked, the same words in both modes.
d = json['{"i": 1, "k": "b", "n": 5, "x": 2.5, "flag": true, "t": "2026-07-14T09:30:00Z", "s": "7"}']
xs = [10, 20, 30]
log[xs[d.i]]
m = map[a = 1, b = 2]
log[m[d.k]]
log[d.n gt 1]
log[d.n + 1]
log[d.x * 2.0]
total = 0
total = d.n
log[total]
log[upper[d.k]]
if d.flag
    log['decided']
log[not d.flag]
log[d.flag and true]
log[d.k eq 'b']
log[d.n eq 5]
log[d.t eq moment['2026-07-14T09:30:00Z']]
--- text that reads as a number is a number where one is met
log[d.s + 1]
fn twice[n]
    return n * 2
log[twice[d.n]]
--- two parsed values compare as the program runs, in order too, and two
--- met in arithmetic are both numbers
log[d.i eq d.n]
log[d.n gt d.i]
log[d.k gt d.s]
log[d.i + d.n]
bad = json['{"n": "many"}']
log[bad.n + 1]
